```

### Test

```bash
make test
```

### Test coverage

```bash
make test-cov
```

Prints a terminal summary and writes `lcov.info` at the project root. The
[Coverage Gutters](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ryanluker.vscode-coverage-gutters)
VS Code extension (preinstalled in the devcontainer) reads `lcov.info` and
highlights covered / uncovered lines in the editor gutter — run **Coverage
Gutters: Display Coverage** from the command palette, or click *Watch* in the
status bar.

CI uploads `lcov.info` to [Codecov](https://codecov.io) on every push. To show
a live coverage badge in this README, sign in at codecov.io with GitHub, enable
this repo, and add the badge near the top:

```markdown
[![Coverage](https://codecov.io/gh/<OWNER>/<REPO>/branch/main/graph/badge.svg)](https://codecov.io/gh/<OWNER>/<REPO>)
```

### Run the full quality gate

`make check` runs the same pre-commit suite CI runs — file hygiene, ruff
lint + format, codespell, bandit, gitleaks, mypy, and pytest:

```bash
make check
```

## Docker

Dev stack:

```bash
make docker-up        # start (detached)
make docker-logs      # tail logs
make docker-down      # stop and remove
```

Prod stack (applies `docker-compose.prod.yml` overrides):

```bash
make docker-up-prod
make docker-down-prod
```

Run `make help` to see every target.

## Diagrams

PlantUML diagrams live in `docs/diagrams/`. Render to PNG:

```bash
make diagrams
```

## Release

Tag and push a release:

```bash
make release VERSION=1.0.0
```

